# The clipboard out of a movie, and FileReference (cavekit-flash.md R7), on the instrumented movie. The system
# clipboard is primed with a text of the script's own; a press on the movie's left band calls
# System.setClipboard("jihad-clip-7391"); the page's own field is then held and Paste tapped in the card's menu.
# THE LIMIT, recorded (T-658, 2026-11-16): the movie's text does not reach the system clipboard, in the stock
# browser either (docs/rounds/t658-2026-11-16): libflashplayer.so imports nothing of it, its Clipboard is its own.
# So the checks are that the system clipboard still holds the primed text after the movie's call and that Paste
# puts exactly that in the page's field: the day the movie's text arrives, this script fails and the limit's note
# comes out of the kit. The middle and right bands call FileReference.browse() and .download(): this player has
# no file dialog, both answer false, and no dialog and no download may come.
id: flash-clipboard-out
section: Flash
item: A movie's System.setClipboard runs and leaves the system clipboard as it was (the player's clipboard is its own, in the stock browser too): Paste in a page field beside the movie gives the text copied before; FileReference.browse and .download answer false in this player and start nothing
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-flash-instr.html?movie=text&clip=1
kit: cavekit-flash.md R7
wait text ready stage= 30
clipboard-set jihad-prime-41
flash-tap m 400 300 showAll 60 260
wait text clip "clip set" 6
expect clipboard jihad-prime-41
tap pf
expect keyboard up 8
hold-on pf 1500
wait line 'hold at .* editable=1' 6
shoot menu
chrome field-paste
wait text pfv "pf jihad-prime-41" 8
chrome kb-hide
expect keyboard down 8
flash-tap m 400 300 showAll 200 260
wait text file "file browse false" 6
flash-tap m 400 300 showAll 330 260
wait text file "file download false" 6
wait quiet 'jihad-dl\|dialog ' 4
